WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.286
JAMIE: The compliance officer I
pictured earlier? She's now

00:00:02.286 --> 00:00:04.572
JAMIE: on her third coffee and
she's drawn a

00:00:04.572 --> 00:00:06.858
JAMIE: very large diagram.

00:00:06.923 --> 00:00:08.295
RUFUS: With several question marks
where the arrows should

00:00:08.295 --> 00:00:09.667
RUFUS: be.

00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:12.324
JAMIE: Though a domestic model's
servers being in Palo

00:00:12.324 --> 00:00:14.768
JAMIE: Alto isn't the same legal
and jurisdictional risk

00:00:14.768 --> 00:00:17.212
JAMIE: as servers subject to
Chinese law.

00:00:17.277 --> 00:00:18.436
RUFUS: No, that's a fair
distinction.

00:00:18.616 --> 00:00:21.162
ALEX: And AP is clear this is a
federal

00:00:21.162 --> 00:00:23.709
ALEX: civilian-agency action. Not
a consumer ban. But if

00:00:23.709 --> 00:00:26.255
ALEX: you sell software to the
federal government, you

00:00:26.255 --> 00:00:28.801
ALEX: need to audit whether
DeepSeek is anywhere in

00:00:28.801 --> 00:00:31.348
ALEX: your stack — because if it
is, you

00:00:31.348 --> 00:00:33.894
ALEX: have a procurement problem.
